<node id="paper::broad_0f37082c3176a42aa3ff::claim_ru_support_synergy">
  <data key="d4">MechanismClaim</data>
  <data key="d5">The Ru–O–W interfacial anchoring and strong metal–support interaction produce an electron-deficient Ru cluster state with modulated Ru–H strength, while W18O49 provides a potential proton-migration channel; these effects collectively enable efficient acidic HER and HOR catalysis.</data>
  <data key="d18">support-induced bifunctional electrocatalysis mechanism</data>
  <data key="d19">The Ru–O–W interfacial anchoring and strong metal–support interaction produce an electron-deficient Ru cluster state with modulated Ru–H strength, while W18O49 provides a potential proton-migration channel; these effects collectively enable efficient acidic HER and HOR catalysis.</data>
  <data key="d20">mixed</data>
  <data key="d6">Mechanistic interpretation explicitly attributed to microstructural analyses, X-ray absorption spectroscopy, and DFT calculations.</data>
  <data key="d7">["claim_ru_support_synergy"]</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">broad_mechanism_abstract</data>
